{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-9-1","title":"Job 9:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job acknowledges God's justice. 22 Man's innocency is not to be condemned by afflictions.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-2","title":"Job 9:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>how. 4:17; 14:3,4; 25:4; 32:2; 33:9; 34:5; 1Ki 8:46; Ps 130:3; 143:2 Ro 3:20 with. or, before.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-3","title":"Job 9:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>he will contend. 20,32,33; 10:2; 23:3-7; 31:35-37; 33:13; 34:14,15; 40:2 Isa 57:15,16; Ro 9:20 he cannot. Ps 19:12; 40:12; 1Jo 1:8; 3:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-4","title":"Job 9:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>wise in heart. 19; 36:5; Ps 104:24; 136:5; Da 2:20; 4:34-37; Ro 11:33; Eph 1:8,19 Eph 3:10,20; Jude 1:24,25 who hath hardened. 6:10; 15:23-27; 40:9; Ex 9:14-17; 14:17,18; Pr 28:14; 29:1 Da 5:20-30; 1Co 10:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-5","title":"Job 9:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>removeth. 28:9; Ps 46:2; 68:8; 114:6; Isa 40:12; Hab 3:6,10; Zec 4:7; Mt 21:21 1Co 13:2; Re 6:14; 11:13 which overturneth. Nu 1:5,6; Zec 14:4,5; Mt 27:51; Lu 21:11; Re 16:18-20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-6","title":"Job 9:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>shaketh. Isa 2:19,21; 13:13,14; 24:1,19,20; Hag 2:6,21; Heb 12:26; Re 20:11 the pillars. 26:11; 38:4-7; 1Sa 2:8; Ps 75:3; 114:7; Jer 4:24; Joe 2:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-7","title":"Job 9:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>commandeth. Ex 10:21,22; Jos 10:12; Da 4:35; Am 4:13; 8:9; Mt 24:29 sealeth. 37:7; 38:12-15,19,20; Isa 13:10; Eze 32:7; Lu 21:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-8","title":"Job 9:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Which. 37:18; Ge 1:6,7; Ps 33:6; 104:2,3; Isa 40:22; 42:5; 44:24; Jer 10:11 Zec 12:1 treadeth. 38:11; Ps 93:3,4; Mt 14:25-30; Joh 6:19 waves. Heb. heights.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-9","title":"Job 9:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>maketh. 38:31,32-41; Ge 1:16; Ps 147:4; Am 5:8 Arcturus, Orion, and Pleiades. Heb. Ash, Cesil, and Cimah.the chambers. Ps 104:3,13; Ac 28:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-10","title":"Job 9:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>great things. 5:9; 26:12-14; 37:23; Ps 71:15; 72:18; Ec 3:11; Isa 40:26-28 Ro 11:33; Eph 3:20 wonders. Ex 15:11; Ps 136:4; Da 4:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-11","title":"Job 9:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>he goeth. 23:8,9; 35:14; Ps 77:19; 1Ti 6:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-12","title":"Job 9:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>he taketh. 23:13; 34:29; Da 4:35; Eph 1:11 hinder him. Heb. turn him away. 11:10 What. 33:13; Isa 45:9; Jer 18:6; Mt 11:26; 20:15; Ro 9:18-20; 11:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-13","title":"Job 9:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>the proud helpers. Heb. the helpers of pride, or strength. 26:12; 40:9-11; Isa 30:7; 31:2,3; Jas 4:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-14","title":"Job 9:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>How much. 4:19; 25:6; 1Ki 8:27 shall I. 11:4,5 choose. 23:4,7; 33:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-15","title":"Job 9:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>though. 10:15; 1Co 4:4 I would. 5:8; 8:5; 10:2; 22:27; 34:31,32; 1Ki 8:38,39; 2Ch 33:13; Jer 31:9 Da 9:3,18 my judge. 23:7; 1Pe 2:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-16","title":"Job 9:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>If I had. Ps 18:6; 66:18-20; 116:1,2 would I. 29:24; Ex 6:9; Jud 6:13; Ps 126:1; Lu 24:41; Ac 12:14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-17","title":"Job 9:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>For he. 16:14; Ps 29:5; 42:7; 83:15; Isa 28:17; Jer 23:19; Eze 13:13 Mt 7:27; 12:20 multiplieth. 1:14-19; 2:7,13 without cause. 2:3; 16:17; 34:6; Ps 25:3; Joh 9:3; 15:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-18","title":"Job 9:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>will not. 7:19; Ps 39:13; 88:7,15-18; La 3:3,18 filleth me. 3:20; La 3:15,19; Heb 12:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-19","title":"Job 9:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>he is strong. 4; 36:17-19; 40:9,10; Ps 62:11; Mt 6:13; 1Co 1:25; 10:22 who shall. 32,33; 31:35; 33:5-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-20","title":"Job 9:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>justify. 2; 4:17; 32:1,2; Ps 130:3; 143:2; Lu 10:29; 16:15 mine. 15:5,6; 34:35; 35:16; Pr 10:19; Isa 6:5; Mt 12:36,37; Jas 3:2 I am perfect. 1:1; Php 3:12-15 it shall. 33:8-13; Pr 17:20; 1Ti 6:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-21","title":"Job 9:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>yet would. Ps 139:23,24; Pr 28:26; Jer 17:9,10; 1Co 4:4; 1Jo 3:20 I would. 7:15,16,21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-22","title":"Job 9:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>He destroyeth. Ec 9:1-3; Eze 21:3,4; Lu 13:2-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-23","title":"Job 9:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>If the. 1:13-19; 2:7 he will. 4:7; 8:20; 2Sa 14:15,17; Ps 44:22; Eze 14:19-21; 21:13 Heb 11:36,37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-24","title":"Job 9:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>earth. 12:6-10; 21:7-15; Ps 17:14; 73:3-7; Jer 12:1,2; Da 4:17; 5:18-21 Da 7:7-28; Hab 1:14-17 he covereth. 2Sa 15:30; 19:4; Es 6:12; 7:8; Jer 14:4 if not. 24:25; 32:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-25","title":"Job 9:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>swifter. 7:6,7; Es 8:14 a post.{Rotz,} a runner, or courier; some of whom are said to go 150 miles in less than 24 hours.</p>\n<p>they flee away. Ps 39:5,11; 89:47; 90:9,10; Jas 4:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-26","title":"Job 9:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>swift ships. Heb. ships of desire, or, ships of Ebeh. asthe eagle. 39:27-30; 2Sa 1:23; Pr 23:5; Jer 4:13; La 4:19; Hab 1:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-27","title":"Job 9:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>7:13; Ps 77:2,3; Jer 8:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-28","title":"Job 9:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>afraid. 21:6; Ps 88:15,16; 119:120 I know. 2,20,21; 14:16; Ex 20:7; Ps 130:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-29","title":"Job 9:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>22; 10:7,14-17; 21:16,17,27; 22:5-30; Ps 73:13; Jer 2:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-30","title":"Job 9:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>Ps 26:6; Pr 28:13; Isa 1:16-18; Jer 2:22; 4:14; Ro 10:3; 1Jo 1:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-31","title":"Job 9:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>shalt. 20; 15:6 mine. Isa 59:6; 64:6; Php 3:8,9 abhor me. or, make me to be abhorred.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-32","title":"Job 9:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>not a man. 33:12; 35:5-7; Nu 23:19; 1Sa 16:7; Ec 6:10; Isa 45:9; Jer 49:19 Ro 9:20; 1Jo 3:20 we should. 13:18-23; 23:3-7; Ps 143:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-33","title":"Job 9:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>is there. 19; 1Sa 2:25; Ps 106:23; 1Jo 2:1,2 daysman. Heb. one that should argue, or, umpire. thatmight. 1Ki 3:16-28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-9-34","title":"Job 9:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>let not. 13:11,20-22; 23:15; 31:23; 33:7; 37:1; Ps 39:10; 90:11 but it is not so with me. Heb. but I am not so with myself. 29:2-25</p>"}]}